Mon Oct 26 11:14:32 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.17.0 (upstream tag v0.17.0, 2026-10-25):
  * New: heavy plug-in filters allowed at install and run in the
    background; OpenType SVG colour fonts draw and export as
    vector art; Constrain Angle for arrow keys, Shift drags and new
    objects; Artboard Options centre mark and cross hairs; Simplify
    slider opens at the Auto-Simplify level; SVG import/export keeps
    other applications' attributes; Place and Export for Screens
    decode, encode and write on background threads.
  * Fixes: brush output budget across tracks, tiles and copies;
    paragraph Auto Leading and hanging punctuation under Glyph
    Scaling; PDF import tracking and glyph widths; pastes follow
    Draw Inside and Draw Behind; Windows Ink pen barrel button.
  * Hardening: font collection face count and live Pathfinder
    effect input capped; render depth counters restored after a
    caught panic.
  * Re-vendor locked (update=false retained); licence audit redone,
    no new licences in the linked set (r-efi, an OR alternative
    with LGPL-2.1-or-later, is used under MIT).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Oct 23 07:14:46 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.16.0 (upstream tag v0.16.0, 2026-10-23):
  * Covers 0.14.0 (2026-10-21) and 0.15.0 (2026-10-22) too.
  * New: Objects on Path; Effect Gallery and many more Sketch and
    Artistic raster filters; Hard Mix and Soft Mix effects;
    tangent and perpendicular snapping; dithered and perceptual
    (OKLab) gradients; ruby and COLR/bitmap colour emoji fonts;
    Insert Kashidas and Optical Margin Alignment; artboard
    background colours; dock group improvements; Targa (.tga)
    open and place; linked PDF/.ai place; Affinity import of
    strokes, text and CMYK photos; export progress with Cancel.
  * CLI and MCP: run --commands reads steps from a JSON file or
    stdin; automation read/write roots may be given repeatedly;
    exports honour SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH.
  * Linux: Wayland window decorations through craft-window and
    sctk-adwaita (no title font); Save As takes the file type
    from the desktop portal dialog; pen barrel buttons work;
    desktop file and MIME XML now register .vectorcraft,
    templates, .ai, EPS, Affinity and the other openable types.
  * Hardening (no CVE ids): deep XMP and SVG image nesting
    capped, mesh and repeat instance limits, numbers given as
    text refused by commands, owner-only recovery folders and
    browser preview folders, links on other shares not followed.
  * New interface languages: Georgian and Turkish.
  * Re-vendor locked (update=false retained): new craft-window
    git pin, chrono 0.4.45 and sctk-adwaita 0.10.1 added, plus
    routine bumps (zerocopy, zvariant, toml, libc, serde_json and
    others), all MIT and/or Apache-2.0, some with Unicode-3.0 or a
    BSD-2-Clause alternative. License re-audit over shipped targets
    unchanged, still no copyleft linked; cargo_vendor reports all
    lockfiles audited, no RUSTSEC advisories.
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list.
- Legal-Review-Notice: list zlib-rs instead of slotmap (not linked
  on Linux), note sctk-adwaita is built without its Cantarell
  title font, and state that colored (MPL-2.0) in the vendor set
  is a never-built dev-dependency.

